course: dictionary
lesson: 2677
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the writer wants. Look at the words before and after it, and ask: what is this text about? «The diaphragm is a muscle under the lungs that helps us breathe in.» The words lungs and breathe are the clues, so diaphragm means a muscle in your body.
explain: Diaphragm has a second meaning too: a thin sheet or disc that moves or vibrates, such as in a microphone or speaker. A science text about the body means the muscle. A text about sound equipment means the disc. The topic is the clue.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «When the diaphragm tightens and moves down, the chest gets bigger and air flows into the lungs.» If you put "thin disc in a speaker" there, it does not make sense, so the muscle meaning is right.
fact: The diaphragm is a large, flat, dome-shaped muscle under your lungs.
fact: The diaphragm helps you breathe: it moves down when you breathe in and up when you breathe out.
fact: A diaphragm can also be a thin sheet or disc that moves or vibrates, such as in a microphone or speaker.
fact: In music, singers breathe «from the diaphragm».
fact: A hiccup happens when the diaphragm suddenly jerks.
exercise: «The diaphragm is a muscle under the lungs that helps us breathe in.» What is a diaphragm here? | A thin disc in a speaker | A kind of drink | *A muscle that helps you breathe | A bone in the chest
exercise: Mia reads: «The diaphragm of the microphone shook when Sam sang.» What does diaphragm mean here? | A type of food | A muscle under the lungs | *A thin disc that vibrates | A breathing tube
exercise: «A hiccup is the diaphragm, the big breathing muscle under the lungs, suddenly jerking.» Which word is the clue that diaphragm means a body part? | jerking | hiccup | *lungs
test: «When the diaphragm tightens and moves down, the chest gets bigger.» What does the diaphragm do here? | It turns into a thin disc | It hides under the ribs | It makes sound through a speaker | *It moves down and makes the chest bigger
test: A singing teacher says, «Breathe from your diaphragm.» What does she mean? | *Breathe deeply, using the muscle under your lungs | Breathe through your nose only | Hold your breath for as long as you can | Sing into a microphone
exam: «The diaphragm of the speaker was cracked.» What does diaphragm mean? | A bone in the chest | *A thin disc that vibrates | A muscle under the lungs | A type of breath
